From 6b994ecb7b72e8cc0c31bda2cc9d27f734e919e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:27:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] avcodec/vc1_mc: fix FASTUVMC rounding of interpolated
 backward chroma MVs

With FASTUVMC set, chroma motion vectors are rounded to the nearest
half-pel position towards zero (SMPTE 421M 8.3.5.4.5). ff_vc1_mc_1mv()
and ff_vc1_mc_4mv_chroma() do that, but ff_vc1_interp_mc() rounds the
backward chroma vector of interpolated B macroblocks away from zero,
which shifts their chroma by a quarter pel whenever the vector is odd.

Use the same rounding as the other two functions. Decoded B pictures
now match the SMPTE reference decoder.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 libavcodec/vc1_mc.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/vc1_mc.c b/libavcodec/vc1_mc.c
index db19d95ef934..d64f2e671035 100644
--- a/libavcodec/vc1_mc.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vc1_mc.c
@@ -1027,8 +1027,8 @@ void ff_vc1_interp_mc(VC1Context *v)
         uvmy = uvmy - 2 + 4 * v->cur_field_type;
     }
     if (v->fastuvmc) {
-        uvmx = uvmx + ((uvmx < 0) ? -(uvmx & 1) : (uvmx & 1));
-        uvmy = uvmy + ((uvmy < 0) ? -(uvmy & 1) : (uvmy & 1));
+        uvmx = uvmx + ((uvmx < 0) ? (uvmx & 1) : -(uvmx & 1));
+        uvmy = uvmy + ((uvmy < 0) ? (uvmy & 1) : -(uvmy & 1));
     }
     srcY = s->next_pic.data[0];
     srcU = s->next_pic.data[1];

From f4cee765dde1edf1f979a6850d948428a855d1fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:27:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] avcodec/vc1_pred: pull back the co-located MV of
 Simple/Main direct mode

For Simple and Main profile B pictures, the co-located motion vector of
direct mode macroblocks is pulled back like a chroma vector before it
is scaled (SMPTE 421M 8.4.5.5, vc1DERIVEMV_DirectMV() and
vc1CROPMV_ChromaPullBack() of the reference decoder). Without it, direct
macroblocks at the picture edges predict from the wrong place.

Fixes the B pictures of the SMM0005 conformance stream, which now match
the SMPTE reference decoder.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 libavcodec/vc1_pred.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/vc1_pred.c b/libavcodec/vc1_pred.c
index 1ac8f6156b19..26bdadb7fe06 100644
--- a/libavcodec/vc1_pred.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vc1_pred.c
@@ -722,10 +722,36 @@ void ff_vc1_pred_b_mv(VC1Context *v, int dmv_x[2], int dmv_y[2],
     if (direct && s->next_pic.ptr->field_picture)
         av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_WARNING, "Mixed frame/field direct mode not supported\n");
 
-    s->mv[0][0][0] = scale_mv(s->next_pic.motion_val[1][xy][0], v->bfraction, 0, s->quarter_sample);
-    s->mv[0][0][1] = scale_mv(s->next_pic.motion_val[1][xy][1], v->bfraction, 0, s->quarter_sample);
-    s->mv[1][0][0] = scale_mv(s->next_pic.motion_val[1][xy][0], v->bfraction, 1, s->quarter_sample);
-    s->mv[1][0][1] = scale_mv(s->next_pic.motion_val[1][xy][1], v->bfraction, 1, s->quarter_sample);
+    {
+        int col_x = s->next_pic.motion_val[1][xy][0];
+        int col_y = s->next_pic.motion_val[1][xy][1];
+
+        /*
+         * Simple/Main profile: the co-located motion vector is pulled back
+         * like a chroma vector before it is scaled (SMPTE reference decoder,
+         * vc1DERIVEMV_DirectMV() -> vc1CROPMV_ChromaPullBack()).
+         */
+        if (v->profile < PROFILE_ADVANCED) {
+            int ix = s->mb_x * 8 + (col_x >> 2);
+            int iy = s->mb_y * 8 + (col_y >> 2);
+            int w  = s->mb_width  * 8;
+            int h  = s->mb_height * 8;
+
+            if (ix < -8)
+                col_x -= 4 * (ix + 8);
+            else if (ix > w)
+                col_x -= 4 * (ix - w);
+            if (iy < -8)
+                col_y -= 4 * (iy + 8);
+            else if (iy > h)
+                col_y -= 4 * (iy - h);
+        }
+
+        s->mv[0][0][0] = scale_mv(col_x, v->bfraction, 0, s->quarter_sample);
+        s->mv[0][0][1] = scale_mv(col_y, v->bfraction, 0, s->quarter_sample);
+        s->mv[1][0][0] = scale_mv(col_x, v->bfraction, 1, s->quarter_sample);
+        s->mv[1][0][1] = scale_mv(col_y, v->bfraction, 1, s->quarter_sample);
+    }
 
     /* Pullback predicted motion vectors as specified in 8.4.5.4 */
     s->mv[0][0][0] = av_clip(s->mv[0][0][0], -60 - (s->mb_x << 6), (s->mb_width  << 6) - 4 - (s->mb_x << 6));

From 8feb356396399b62401123ba4981d9a955656c7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@siol.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:39:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] avcodec/vc1: read RESPIC only in I and P pictures

RESPIC is present in Simple and Main profile I and P pictures only
(SMPTE 421M 7.1.1.23, and the SMPTE reference decoder); B and BI
pictures keep the value of the last I or P picture. The B check missed
BI pictures, which are signalled as B pictures with BFRACTION = 0 and
have been turned into AV_PICTURE_TYPE_BI by then, so 2 bits too many
were read from the header of every BI picture of a MULTIRES sequence.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@siol.net>
---
 libavcodec/vc1.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/vc1.c b/libavcodec/vc1.c
index ab247f0a7f26..33ff7af35851 100644
--- a/libavcodec/vc1.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vc1.c
@@ -696,7 +696,8 @@ int ff_vc1_parse_frame_header(VC1Context *v, GetBitContext* gb)
     v->k_y = v->mvrange + 8; //k_y can be 8 9 10 11
     v->range_x = 1 << (v->k_x - 1);
     v->range_y = 1 << (v->k_y - 1);
-    if (v->multires && v->s.pict_type != AV_PICTURE_TYPE_B)
+    if (v->multires && (v->s.pict_type == AV_PICTURE_TYPE_I ||
+                        v->s.pict_type == AV_PICTURE_TYPE_P))
         v->respic = get_bits(gb, 2);
 
     if (v->res_x8 && (v->s.pict_type == AV_PICTURE_TYPE_I || v->s.pict_type == AV_PICTURE_TYPE_BI)) {

From 9632e3bf306d269c771cd80ce924442db899e61b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@siol.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] avcodec/vc1: size the bitplanes of reduced resolution
 pictures

A Simple or Main profile picture of a MULTIRES sequence may be coded at
half the width and/or half the height of the sequence (RESPIC). Its
bitplanes have one bit per macroblock of the picture as coded, so
decoding them with the macroblock size of the sequence reads the wrong
number of bits and desyncs the rest of the picture header.

The macroblock layer of such pictures is still decoded at the size of
the sequence, which this does not change, but the header is now parsed
correctly, which is what hardware decoders need.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@siol.net>
---
 libavcodec/vc1.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavcodec/vc1.c b/libavcodec/vc1.c
index 33ff7af35851..fc7b45d663f7 100644
--- a/libavcodec/vc1.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vc1.c
@@ -102,6 +102,13 @@ static int bitplane_decoding(uint8_t* data, int *raw_flag, VC1Context *v)
 
     width  = v->s.mb_width;
     height = v->s.mb_height >> v->field_mode;
+    /* RESPIC: Simple/Main picture coded at half width and/or height */
+    if (v->profile < PROFILE_ADVANCED && v->multires) {
+        if (v->respic & 1)
+            width  = (v->s.width  / 2 + 15) >> 4;
+        if (v->respic & 2)
+            height = (v->s.height / 2 + 15) >> 4;
+    }
     stride = v->s.mb_stride;
     invert = get_bits1(gb);
     imode = get_vlc2(gb, ff_vc1_imode_vlc, VC1_IMODE_VLC_BITS, 1);

From f5058c6f7cb499c5ce392673531c6972f84d7d9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:19:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] avcodec: add V4L2 Request API VC-1/WMV3 hwaccel

Add a stateless V4L2 Request API hwaccel for VC-1 and WMV3 (SMPTE 421M
Simple, Main and Advanced profiles), for the V4L2_PIX_FMT_VC1_SLICE
pixel format and the VC-1 stateless controls:

  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_SEQUENCE
  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_ENTRYPOINT_HEADER
  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_PICTURE_LAYER
  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_BITPLANES
  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_SLICE_PARAMS (if the driver has it)

One request is queued per coded picture, that is, per frame or per
field of a field-interlaced frame. The output buffer holds the picture
as in the bitstream: with its start codes and emulation prevention
bytes for the Advanced profile, as carried by the container for the
Simple and Main profiles.

The controls describe the reference pictures explicitly (picture types,
frame coding mode, range reduction, and the intensity compensation
which earlier pictures applied to each reference field). The decoder
only keeps the intensity compensation as look-up tables, so the hwaccel
tracks the syntax elements itself, next to the controls of each picture.

Skipped pictures are not queued: the frame is made to share the buffers
of its reference, which is thereby output again. Each picture of a
packet is queued without the BDUs which follow it.

Streams of the pre-release bitstream formats which STRUCT_C announces
(RES_X8, a clear RES_FASTTX) are refused; RES_RTM is passed as a flag
and left to the driver.

Streams which need range expansion (Main profile RANGERED) or range
mapping (Advanced profile) are left to software, because the capture
buffer holds the picture before those output processes and nothing
applies them yet.

A reduced resolution (RESPIC) picture of a MULTIRES sequence is decoded
at its coded size into the top-left corner of the frame, as the kernel
API specifies; its bitplanes are passed at that size. Upsampling it,
which SMPTE 421M leaves to the implementation, is not done yet (the
software decoder does not handle RESPIC at all).

The controls are not part of the kernel headers yet: a private copy of
their definitions is in v4l2-stateless-vc1.h.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
